                <pb facs="1042" n="928" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg928"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.4016/517: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Athens</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-03T16:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 3, 1922—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>75. The Minister for Foreign Affairs asked me to telegraph Department: “Greek
                    Government earnestly hopes for American participation on commissions to
                    investigate Asia Minor atrocities.”</p>
                <p>[Paraphrase.] It is my opinion that the Greek Government is very anxious to have
                    the United States participate but that the Minister for Foreign Affairs is not
                    very hopeful that the Department will act on his request. [End paraphrase.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
